the exclusive diffractive production of vector mesons and real photons in @xmath0 collisions has been studied at hera in a wide kinematic range . here 
 we present the most recent experimental results together with a regge - type model . 
 we deduce the pomeranchuk trajectory ( pomeron ) by analyzing the hera data on deeply virtual compton scattering ( dvcs ) , and then discuss its basic properties , namely its apparent hardnessand its non - flatbehavior , different from the claims of some authors . 
